{"id":"word:hebrew:H5291","type":"word","title":"נַעֲרָה","subtitle":"H5291 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a girl (from infancy to adolescence)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נַעֲרָה (H5291) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 76 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נַעֲרָה (naʻărâh) means a girl (from infancy to adolescence) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 1 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נַעֲרָה","transliteration":"naʻărâh","pronunciation":"nah-ar-aw'","strong":"H5291","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5291","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["ה/נער","נַעֲרָ֣ה","הַֽ/נַּעֲרָ֔ה","הַֽ/נַּעֲרָ֖ה","הַֽ/נַּעֲרָה֙"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncfsa",35],["HNcfsa",11],["HRd/Ncfsa",5],["HC/Td/Ncfsa",4],["HNcfpa",3],["HNcfpc/Sp3fs",3],["HC/Rd/Ncfsa",2],["HC/Ncfpc/Sp3fs",2],["HR/Ncfpc/Sp2ms",2],["HNcfpc/Sp3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a girl (from infancy to adolescence)","usage":"damsel, maid(-en), young (woman).","full":"H5291. naarah II. נַעֲרָה noun feminine girl, damsel ; — absolute ׳נ Judg 19:3 22 t., also Qr Gen 24:14 20 t. Genesis, Deuteronomy ( נַעֲרָה Kt in Pentateuch only Deut 22:19 , see below); plural absolute נְעָרוֺת 1Sam 9:11 +, construct נַעֲרוֺת Est 4:4 ; suffix נַעֲרוֺתָיו Ruth 2:22 ; 3:2 , נַעֲרֹתֶיהָ Gen 24:61 ; Exod 2:5 , etc.; &#8212; 1 girl, damsel ; ׳נ קְטַנָּה little girl only 2Kin 5:2 , compare 5:4 , perhaps = young daughters Job 40:29; elsewhere = young woman 1Sam 9:11 ; especially as marriageable, Gen 24:14 , 16 , 28 , 55 , 57 ; 34:3 , 12 (all J), Deut 22:15 (twice in verse); 22:16 , 19 , 20 , 21 , 24 , 26 (twice in verse); 22:29 ; 1Kin 1:3-4 , Est 2:4 , 7 , 8 , 9 , 12 (twice in verse); 2:13 ; specifically virgin ׳נ בְּתוּלָה Judg 21:12 ; Deut 22:23 , 28 ; 1Kin 1:2 ; Est 2:2-3 ,(compare Deut 22:15 b; 22:20 ); ׳נ מְאֹרָשָׂה betrothed girl 22:25 , 27 ; young widow Ruth 2:6 ; 4:12 ; of a concubine Judg 19:3-4 , 5 , 6 , 8 , 9 , a prostitute Amos 2:7 . 2 of female attendants , maids (always plural), Gen 24:61 (J), Exod 2:5 (E), 1Sam 25:42 ; Prov 9:3 ; 27:27 ; 31:15 ; Est 2:9 (twice in verse); 4:4 , 16 ; gleaners Ruth 2:5 , 8 , 22 , 23 ; 3:2 . &#8212; Note. נער Kt in Pentateuch as feminine (Qr נַעֲרָ֯ ) is probably not original; it is not found in Sam. Pentateuch, and feminine plural נַעֲרֹתֶיהָ occurs Genesis, Exodus; compare Ges §§ 2n , 17c.","rootNote":"feminine of 5288 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 1 2","keyReferences":["1Kgs 1 2","1Kgs 1 3","1Kgs 1 4","1Sam 9 11","1Sam 25 42","2Kgs 5 2","2Kgs 5 4","Amos 2 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":76,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 1 2","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַעֲרָ֣ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 3","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַעֲרָ֣ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 4","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַֽ/נַּעֲרָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 9 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":9,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נְעָר֔וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 42","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַעֲרֹתֶ֔י/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"2Kgs 5 2","book":"2Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נַעֲרָ֣ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"2Kgs 5 4","book":"2Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַֽ/נַּעֲרָ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Amos 2 7","book":"Amos","chapter":2,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַֽ/נַּעֲרָ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Deut 22 15","book":"Deut","chapter":22,"verse":15,"eng